Run a replacement wherever one path is executed (boot-arg nx769j-execswap=<path>=<replacement>[,<path>=<replacement>]).

exec_activate_image saves the copied-in path, then, when it equals <path> exactly, saves <replacement> in its place before the
lookup. With the boot-arg set, every exec below /private/var/ngpu/bin/ is marked IMGPF_NX769J_EXECSWAP. For a marked image
mac_vnode_check_exec ignores the platform Sandbox verdict (the Sandbox refuses exec from the Data volume) and process_signature
ignores the launch-constraint refusal (the owner trust module gives no constraint category); AMFI's signature checks and the
other policies still decide. A marked exec that fails prints its stage and uid, every MAC policy that refused it in
vnode_check_exec, and a signature or launch-constraint refusal. The first swaps are logged as "NX769J EXECSWAP".

